#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vault-lint — validator and GTD review for a tidyvault Obsidian vault.

Enforces Agents/schema.md (the frontmatter contract) plus the structural,
GTD, linking, attachment and body-section rules in Agents/. The rule-by-rule
coverage matrix is in .scripts/README.md. Python 3 standard library only.

USAGE
    python3 .scripts/vault-lint [--fix] [--json] [--only CHECK[,CHECK]]
                                [--quiet] [--root DIR] [--today YYYY-MM-DD]
                                [paths...]
    python3 .scripts/vault-lint --review [--json] [--days N] [--no-git]
                                [--root DIR] [--today YYYY-MM-DD]
    python3 .scripts/vault-lint [--archive-closed] [--promote] [--dry-run]
                                [paths...]

    paths      Limit *reported* findings to these files/folders (relative to
               the vault root or absolute). The whole vault is always indexed
               so links and relations resolve. Dot-folders, _tmp/ (agent
               scratch), _imports/ (files awaiting import), and _captures/ (notes
               awaiting filing) are never indexed.
    --fix      Apply safe mechanical frontmatter rewrites (see FIXES below),
               print what changed, then lint again and report what remains.
    --json     Emit a JSON list of {check, severity, path, line, message,
               fixable} (with --review: one JSON object of review sections).
    --only     Run only the named checks (comma-separated ids). `--only manifest`
               also re-hashes every file the manifest names (slow; sizes are
               checked on every run).
    --quiet    Human output shows errors only (summary still counts all).
    --root     Vault root (default: the folder containing .scripts/).
    --today    Override "today" for date rules and the review.
    --review   Print the GTD daily/weekly review (Agents/gtd.md) as Markdown
               instead of linting: due soon, next actions by project and
               context, inbox, waiting-for ages, next-action rule breaches,
               blocked tasks to promote, stale projects, closed-not-archived,
               Someday/maybe revisits. Always exits 0.
    --days     Due-soon window for --review (default 7).
    --no-git   --review: use file mtimes instead of git history for staleness.

    Exit status: 0 when no errors are reported, 1 when any error is reported,
    2 on usage problems. Warnings and info never fail the run.

CHECKS (stable ids; --list-checks describes them)
    structure, file-format, frontmatter-present, frontmatter-syntax, filename,
    unique-names, title, schema, links, relations, waiting-on, tasks, projects, archive,
    attachments, manifest, anatomy, dataview, dataviewjs, dates, sensitive, format, orphans, facts, source-urls

CONFIG (.tidyvault.yml at the vault root, written by Copier)
    owner, owner_full, owner_slug, vault, store_path, store_image, and the
    modules list (store, pii, false-facts, obsidian, backup). A check whose
    module is off is skipped and listed as off by --list-checks. lint.proper_nouns
    and lint.proper_phrases extend the sentence-case allowlist; lint.disabled_checks
    turns checks off; lint.read_only_url_patterns are regexes for URLs of systems
    agents must never write to (error in frontmatter, info in body). Without the
    file, every module is on and the owner is "the owner".

FIXES (--fix; idempotent, atomic writes)
    reorder keys to schema order · quote bare wikilinks · inline lists to
    block lists · normalise list indent to two spaces · unquote ISO dates in
    date fields · delete empty keys, empty list items and blank lines ·
    delete redundant retired fields (agent_review, edited, archive: false,
    and lint.retired_fields) · strip a UTF-8 byte-order mark. CRLF files keep
    CRLF. A file whose frontmatter has anything outside the restricted subset,
    that isn't valid UTF-8, is a symlink, or changed on disk mid-run is left
    untouched.
    Body formatting (the `format` check; LF notes, not templates): trailing
    spaces, `*`/`+`/`•` bullets to `-`, one blank line around headings, code
    fences, tables and blockquotes, no runs of blank lines, no blank line
    between the frontmatter and the H1, one newline at end of file. Fenced code is never
    touched; wording never changes.

ARCHIVE AND PROMOTE (--archive-closed, --promote; --dry-run shows the plan)
    --archive-closed  Agents/procedures.md, "Archive a file", for each done or
                      cancelled task still in Tasks/: set `completed` (today,
                      when missing), add `archived: true` and `archived_from:
                      Tasks`, move it to Archive/ under the same filename.
                      Closed projects are listed, never moved: archiving one
                      sorts its tasks and Resources, which takes judgment.
    --promote         Agents/gtd.md, "Promote on close": each not-started or
                      in-progress project with no next action gets its best
                      queued task (all blockers closed; highest priority, then
                      earliest due, then oldest created) set to next-action.
                      `contexts` are never guessed: a promoted task without
                      them is reported. Projects with no ready task are listed.
    Both take paths to limit what they touch, run archive first when given
    together, then --fix the files they wrote, and never overwrite: a file
    that changed mid-run, or a taken name in Archive/, is skipped and reported.

ADDING A CHECK
    1. Write `def check_<name>(v: Vault) -> Iterator[Finding]` that yields
       Finding(check=<id>, severity=ERROR|WARNING|INFO, path, line, message).
    2. Decorate it with @check("<id>", "one-line description").
    3. Add good + bad fixtures under .scripts/tests/fixtures, an expectation
       in .scripts/tests/run.py, and a row in the README coverage matrix.
    Schema facts (fields, enums, order) live in the SCHEMA tables below —
    change those, not the checks, when Agents/schema.md changes.
"""

